      <activity id="7a9c8e5e-4785-56c8-9865-abfaeb6273f3" activityNameId="3110bbca-f2ec-509a-bbdf-e26d941be786" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Chlorodifluoromethane, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Chlorodifluoromethane, at plant
Inventory for a chemical. Emissions of HFC-23 are much higher in the world wide average. Emission data from PRTR-database.;
CAS number: 75-45-6; 
Formula: CHClF2; 
Synonyms: HCFC-22, Freon 22, Algeon 22, Isotron 22, Difluorochloromethane, Monochlorodifluoromethane, Refrigerant R22, Fluorocarbon 22, Fisherbrand histo freeze(TM)-22, R-22, Freon R-22, Halocarbon 22, chlorodifluoromethane (R-22), Chlorodifluoromethane; 
UUID: fd9c4fc5-a71e-37bb-ac48-abb578a611ce
Gate to gate inventory for the production in the Netherlands, estimation for infrastructure and not including by-products.
Location: Plant e.g. in NL
Technology: Chemical processing
Time period: undefined
Production volume: The worldwide production capacity in 1987 for fluoroplastics was ca. 45 000t.
Sampling: Literature, company information, stoichiometric calculations, emission database, assumptions. 
Extrapolations: from one plant
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_fd9c4fc5-a71e-37bb-ac48-abb578a611ce.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
